 "captions": [
  [
   0.0,
   1.591,
   "Part two. The architecture."
  ],
  [
   2.223,
   5.405,
   "Before any algorithm, let's see the moving parts."
  ],
  [
   5.905,
   9.405,
   "Your agent talks to one object: the Memory"
  ],
  [
   9.405,
   12.904,
   "API. It exposes add, search, get, update, delete,"
  ],
  [
   12.904,
   13.779,
   "and history."
  ],
  [
   14.41,
   17.91,
   "Behind it sit a few components. An LLM,"
  ],
  [
   17.91,
   20.534,
   "which reads conversations and extracts facts."
  ],
  [
   21.166,
   24.665,
   "An embedder, which turns text into vectors. By"
  ],
  [
   24.665,
   28.164,
   "default, OpenAI's text embedding three small, with fifteen"
  ],
  [
   28.164,
   30.351,
   "hundred and thirty six dimensions."
  ],
  [
   30.983,
   34.482,
   "A vector store holding the memories themselves: Qdrant"
  ],
  [
   34.482,
   37.544,
   "by default, with more than twenty alternatives."
  ],
  [
   38.175,
   41.675,
   "Since twenty twenty six, a second collection holds"
  ],
  [
   41.675,
   42.55,
   "entity records."
  ],
  [
   43.181,
   46.68,
   "And a small SQLite database keeps the history"
  ],
  [
   46.68,
   50.18,
   "of every change, plus the last few messages"
  ],
  [
   50.18,
   51.492,
   "of each session."
  ],
  [
   51.992,
   53.49,
   "Every memory is scoped."
  ],
  [
   54.122,
   57.119,
   "A user id says whose memory it is."
  ],
  [
   57.119,
   60.115,
   "An agent id says which agent it belongs"
  ],
  [
   60.115,
   63.112,
   "to. A run id narrows it to one"
  ],
  [
   63.112,
   64.236,
   "session or task."
  ],
  [
   64.868,
   67.864,
   "You can combine them, and add metadata filters"
  ],
  [
   67.864,
   68.614,
   "on top."
  ],
  [
   69.245,
   72.242,
   "Scoping is enforced on every read and write,"
  ],
  [
   72.242,
   75.239,
   "so one user's memories never leak into another"
  ],
  [
   75.239,
   75.988,
   "user's search."
  ],
  [
   76.62,
   79.616,
   "In the code, identity can only be set"
  ],
  [
   79.616,
   82.239,
   "through these parameters, never through free-form metadata."
  ],
  [
   82.739,
   85.483,
   "What does one memory actually look like?"
  ],
  [
   86.115,
   89.251,
   "In the vector store, it's a point: a"
  ],
  [
   89.251,
   91.211,
   "UUID, and the embedding vector."
  ],
  [
   91.843,
   94.979,
   "Its payload holds the text itself, a hash"
  ],
  [
   94.979,
   98.116,
   "of that text for deduplication, and a lemmatized"
  ],
  [
   98.116,
   100.076,
   "copy used for keyword search."
  ],
  [
   100.708,
   103.844,
   "It also stores the scope, like the user"
  ],
  [
   103.844,
   106.981,
   "id, creation and update timestamps, and an optional"
  ],
  [
   106.981,
   110.117,
   "expiration date, after which the memory is hidden"
  ],
  [
   110.117,
   110.901,
   "from search."
  ],
  [
   111.533,
   114.669,
   "Separately, SQLite logs every change as a history"
  ],
  [
   114.669,
   117.806,
   "row: which memory, the old text, the new"
  ],
  [
   117.806,
   119.766,
   "text, the event, and when."
  ],
  [
   120.266,
   122.573,
   "At runtime there are two paths."
  ],
  [
   123.205,
   126.281,
   "The write path: after each conversation turn, add"
  ],
  [
   126.281,
   128.973,
   "extracts facts, embeds them, and stores them."
  ],
  [
   129.605,
   132.681,
   "The read path: before the agent answers a"
  ],
  [
   132.681,
   135.757,
   "question, search embeds it, ranks memories, and returns"
  ],
  [
   135.757,
   138.065,
   "the top few into the prompt."
  ],
  [
   138.696,
   141.773,
   "Writes can run in the background, off the"
  ],
  [
   141.773,
   144.849,
   "user's critical path. Reads must be fast, because"
  ],
  [
   144.849,
   146.387,
   "the user is waiting."
  ],
  [
   147.019,
   150.095,
   "Keep that asymmetry in mind. It drives nearly"
  ],
  [
   150.095,
   151.249,
   "every design choice."
  ]
 ],
 "audio": "m0/ch02.wav"
}